Z||000011||Songman||07-16-2001||10:10 PM||||Don't count out the Cadillac Evoq that is supposed to debut in 2003! That is one amazing little car. Lots of technology and a 425ho Northstar in a two-seater hardtop convertible!<P>The funny thing is that it is supposed to share a lot of the chassis stuff with the C6 Corvette, but I haven't even been able to find a mention of a C6 Corvette anywhere. It seems like if it was withina year of coming out there should at least be some spy shots or rumors somewhere!<P>Anyway, I love the Evoq, but with a base price of $75,000 it won't be for everyone...<P>I hope GM don't mess up the Corvette like the Lamborghini Diablo got messed up for next year. Do a search and find the spy pictures that are on the net. It has the big ridiculous holes on each side behind the door that look like jet intakes... Crazy!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000012||87ECO5||07-16-2001||10:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>... but I haven't even been able to find a mention of a C6 Corvette anywhere.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>One of the car mags did an article on the C6 a few months ago - complete with artist renditions.  The car on their cover looked a lot like the C5, although the retractable lights (a Vette trademark since '63) are replaced with fixed projectors and some of the lines are sharpened (a la Ford's "New Edge" stuff).||||reg||1
