Z||000015||kslish||07-17-2001||12:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>Don't count out the Cadillac Evoq that is supposed to debut in 2003! That is one amazing little car. Lots of technology and a 425ho Northstar in a two-seater hardtop convertible!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Evoq is going to be built at the Corvette plant in Bowling Green.  They'll roll down the same assembly line (I wonder how Corvette enthusiasts are going to like that). <P>I was looking at some Firebirds at a dealership today since they just got a shipment of 20 or so in.  I've been looking at them ever since GM announced that they were considering doing away with them.  If they truely are stopping production, that purchase may have to come sooner than I had planned.<P>GM seems to be going downhill quick as a car company.  I spent 3 hours Saturday evening at the Michigan Fiero show chatting with the guy that was the last person out of the Fiero plant when it closed down.  He still works for GM and says that there isn't a car guy in the company anymore....it's all corporate execs and accountants.  It was depressing hearing stories of how GM is now starting to subcontract out design work to independent companies to save money (he said the Aztek is a prime example of what results from this kind of management).  The head people at GM just care about the companies stock price and how to make stuff cheaper to build, not better.<P>Ken S.||||reg||1
