Z||000018||Oreif||07-17-2001||03:49 AM||||I don't think they'll use the Firebird or camaro nameplates once they stop production.<BR>Just like the GTO fans, whenever they bring out a prototype and call it a GTO, Pontiac gets flooded with letters and such because they could never make a car to fit the image correctly. Remember when they wanted to downsize the F-bodies into a FWD car that looked like a ford probe? Same result.<P>I think it was one of the Hot Rod magazines that caused a stir when Chevy was going to bring back the "Chevelle" nameplate for the new Malibu's. To many die-hard fans of particular cars won't let the nameplates of the classics be put on cars that would tarnish the image.<P>I think GM learned that lesson with the LeMans and Nova nameplates. Muscle car to korean econo-box. They lasted only a couple of years. ||||reg||1
